 - A change to a record goes to the file of the hub the record is of; a new project, entry, lead, Lit Watch entry or idea goes to the primary hub, else to the first hub of the workspace, and is refused with a sentence only when the workspace lists no hub. A record of the primary hub has a bare id and every record of another hub has the id `<hub name>:<id>` and a chip with the hub name on its card, row or page; with no primary every hub's records carry the prefix. The people, venues, projects and other records an entry names are that hub's own, and a portfolio with one hub that is the primary shows no chip.
 - The `secrets` folder of every hub is private, in any letter case the file system folds: it is withheld from the language servers, the writing rules' folder Fix All and fixes, search and the library rules.
